Z||000002||Joe Torma||10-27-2001||12:46 PM||||Um,er...Probably a vac leak...<P>Unplug the IAC..what happens?<BR>Turn of car,reconnect...<P>Start up...unplug MAP sensor.  What happens?<P>Plug everything back in, and spray carb cleaner on all of the lines.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mach10||10-27-2001||01:34 PM||||O2 sensor/EGR system. Mine did that.... hunts for idle, then drops, almost to stalling, lurches, then slams up to ~2000rpm before starting again...<P>other thing could be your Tps... Try tapping the gas and see if it steadies?||||reg||4
Z||000004||SLYGUY||10-27-2001||09:04 PM||||My GT had a lousy idle till I changed both the EGR and the O2 sesor also!!<BR>My EGR looked original and I know it must of failed the original owner years ago and we won't even talk about how bad the oxy sensor looked when I pulled it. <BR>I can't help it, it looked like a charcoal briquette.<BR>Idle is much better now. Rock solid 800rpm.<BR>Sounds so good I sometimes pull up a lawn chair behind it and just listen for a minute or two!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Sly||||reg||1
